{"status":"completed","summary":"Held curl at 0:8.9.1-5.el10 using RHEL’s supported DNF version-lock plugin. A full update simulation excluded curl despite a newer version being available. The OS release and kernel remained unchanged, and the hold persisted through node1’s verified restart.","actions_performed":["Installed only python3-dnf-plugin-versionlock-4.7.0-8.el10, matching the existing DNF plugin suite.","Added lock curl-0:8.9.1-5.el10.*.","Verified locked and unlocked update behavior and simulated a full system update without applying it.","Removed temporary simulation output and rechecked curl integrity, services, and administrative access.","Restarted node1 once and verified its boot identity changed and all required state recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Keep installed curl at its current version during a system update","command_ids":["cmd-974a60ce6dfd4b21","cmd-c12a3cacfd5741b3","cmd-2dc7156009364a8c"],"summary":"A newer curl 8.12.1 was available, but the active lock suppressed it; a 279-package update simulation contained no curl transaction. Curl remained 0:8.9.1-5.el10 after restart."},{"requirement":"Use a supported, platform-compatible hold mechanism","command_ids":["cmd-057d6d5143f24438","cmd-7edfb16e8c084855","cmd-5ac0b4267d5a4b2d"],"summary":"The exact compatible version-lock plugin required only one 32 kB package, and DNF recorded the installed curl NEVRA."},{"requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-d34f549735d448a2","cmd-7edfb16e8c084855","cmd-2dc7156009364a8c"],"summary":"Only the version-lock plugin was installed. Red Hat release 10.0-30.el10 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 remained installed and running."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart: healthy baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-fb94946f98374de9","cmd-8883289069bc4f2b","cmd-6deed8a089094923","cmd-64e5aa5af7a4493e","cmd-2dc7156009364a8c"],"summary":"Before restart, boot ID was 254597f8-4ac9-4062-8be8-44eba1f6d2e9 with healthy services and intact curl. The reboot was acknowledged, the boot ID changed to 2e891daa-f332-4535-b4a3-99b96c05c746, and the system, SSH, chronyd, curl integrity/functionality, package versions, and version lock fully recovered."}]}
